0,Mungkip language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mungkip_language,"Mungkip language ... Munkip (Mungkip) is a nearly extinct Finisterre languages of Papua New Guinea. It is spoken in Kasuka ( 6.460182°S 146.720285°E) and Mungkip ( 6.478612°S 146.630269°E) villages of Sintogora ward, Wain-Erap Rural LLG. [1]",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
1,Language: Mungkip - transnewguinea.org,https://transnewguinea.org/language/mungkip,"Information: Glottocode: mung1272 ISO 639: mpv Also Known As: Munkip Sources: McElhanon and Voorhoeve (1970) & Retsema et al. (2009) Classification: Nuclear Trans New Guinea, Finisterre-Huon, Finisterre-Saruwaged, Erap, Boana",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
2,"Mungkip Language (MPV) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mpv/,Mungkip is an endangered indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by the elderly only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
3,Variety Mungkip (Nuclear Trans New Guinea) - lexibank.clld.org,https://lexibank.clld.org/languages/transnewguineaorg-mungkip,"Greenhill, Simon J. 2015. TransNewGuinea.org: An Online Database of New Guinea Languages. PLoS ONE 10. e0141563. Public Library of Science.",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
4,Mungkip language - Detailed Pedia,https://www.detailedpedia.com/wiki-Mungkip_language,"It is spoken in Kasuka (6°27′37″S146°43′13″E / 6.460182°S 146.720285°E / -6.460182; 146.720285 (Kasuka)) and Mungkip (6°28′43″S146°37′49″E / 6.478612°S 146.630269°E / -6.478612; 146.630269 (Mungkip)) villages of Sintogora ward, Wain-Erap Rural LLG.",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
5,Mungkip - mossyrune,https://mossyrune.com/language/mungkip,"Mungkip, a language spoken by 12 people. Classification, region, writing system, and what we know about it at a glance.",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
6,Mungkip language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Mungkip_language/,"Munkip (Mungkip) is a nearly extinct Finisterre languages of Papua New Guinea. It is spoken in Kasuka (-6.4602°N 146.7203°W) and Mungkip (-6.4786°N 146.6303°W) villages of Sintogora ward, Wain-Erap Rural LLG.",Mungkip,Trans-New Guinea
